{"name":"Safari Sun","hex":"#b4875e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"safari","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A trip into any undeveloped area to see, photograph or to hunt wild animals in their own environment.","A caravan going on a safari."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take part in a safari."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safari"},{"term":"sun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sundanese."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The star that is closest to the Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun"}],"entries":[{"title":"Safari","blocks":[{"text":"A safari is an overland journey to observe or hunt wild animals, especially in East Africa. The so-called \"Big Five\" game animals of Africa – lion, leopard, rhinoceros, elephant, and Cape buffalo – particularly form an important part of the safari market, both for wildlife viewing and big-game hunting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Sabi_sabi_game_drive.jpg/330px-Sabi_sabi_game_drive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safari"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun"}],"images":[{"srcset"